            <ArticleTitle>Acute coronary stenosis in a young man with Behçet's syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>157-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1159/000112972</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To present a case of myocardial infarction due to Behçet's syndrome.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CLINICAL PRESENTATION AND INTERVENTION" NlmCategory="METHODS">A 27-year-old man who was known to have Behçet's syndrome for 1 year presented with retrosternal fluctuating chest pain, which radiated to the epigastrium 5 h prior to admission. Coronary angiography showed total occlusion of the left anterior descending coronary artery, which was successfully treated with coronary stent implantation.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">This case shows that patients with Behçet's syndrome who had acute chest pain should be thoroughly examined for any signs of acute myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>(c) 2008 S. Karger AG, Basel.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
